WEBVTT

cue0159453
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.320
Thank you very much Susan. Ladies, gentlemen, friends. My managers was the or one of the

cue0159454
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:33.439
greatest men of his time. Usually we know my managers as a great legal mind. The only

cue0159455
00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:45.240
complete code of the entire rabbinic jurisprudence was written by my managers. Every code written

cue0159456
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:58.119
either before or after comprises a small only a small section of rabbinic law. To give you

cue0159457
00:00:58.119 --> 00:01:06.000
an example of what the code of my managers represent, it's a book containing exactly

cue0159458
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:21.360
I counted 1,000 chapters. Each chapter has about 20 paragraphs. Every paragraph contains

cue0159459
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:30.519
between three and five legal decisions. In other words, we're talking about an individual

cue0159460
00:01:30.519 --> 00:01:42.000
who wrote, established the law in about 100,000 cases. But that was only one of the many works

cue0159461
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:51.680
that he did. He's also known as a philosopher. As a matter of fact, they speak of my managers as a

cue0159462
00:01:51.680 --> 00:02:02.199
rationalist. And he was. He was a superb astronomer. In some of his, the chapters of

cue0159463
00:02:02.199 --> 00:02:13.119
the guide, my managers asked questions about the Ptolemyian astronomical system without giving an

cue0159464
00:02:13.119 --> 00:02:20.119
answer. Questions that he asked in disapproval. Questions that several centuries later Copernicus

cue0159465
00:02:20.119 --> 00:02:31.360
would ask. Copernicus asked the same questions, but Copernicus would come to the theory that the

cue0159466
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:39.759
earth turns around the sun. What is important is that my managers in the history of science is the

cue0159467
00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:46.839
first one who point to certain discrepancies in the Ptolemyian system. He was a great physician.

cue0159468
00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:56.720
Today, we are coming back to the medicine of my managers. We believe in three major points about

cue0159469
00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:05.639
medicine. Number one, that medicine has to be basically holistic. You cannot treat a single

cue0159470
00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:13.320
ailment of the body without taking consideration the whole environment in which the individual

cue0159471
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:24.240
lives. He goes to such an extreme as to, as a physician, to ask a patient the color of the walls

cue0159472
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:36.279
of his house to recommend not only medicine, but also music. A holistic concept of medicine. Another

cue0159473
00:03:36.279 --> 00:03:44.919
point which is terribly important in his medicine is the task of the doctor is not to cure, but to

cue0159474
00:03:44.919 --> 00:03:51.880
prevent the human body of becoming sick. A sick person going to a doctor is a failure of a doctor.

cue0159475
00:03:51.880 --> 00:04:03.080
The doctor should not have allowed the patient to become sick. And last but not least, that when the

cue0159476
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:16.119
doctor applies a particular cure, he should make sure that the cure is not worse than the sickness itself,

cue0159477
00:04:16.119 --> 00:04:26.519
the implications of whatever a cure a person might have. A man of great mind. What I want to explore with you

cue0159478
00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:36.679
is an aspect of my managers which is unknown. Those modern scholars who have examined the

cue0159479
00:04:36.679 --> 00:04:45.799
Moreh Neḇukhim deal only with the rationalistic aspect of my managers. And indeed,

cue0159480
00:04:45.799 --> 00:04:54.200
he was rational. But there is something very important about my managers. Let me tell you

cue0159481
00:04:54.200 --> 00:05:06.279
first in a kernel, very briefly, what is my manager's theory of mysticism. And then I will try to show you how it works.

cue0159482
00:05:06.279 --> 00:05:16.079
The most important thing of my managers is that there are three stages in the human development

cue0159483
00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:31.079
as an individual, and in humanity as an anthropological groups. At an early stage, humanity, or we

cue0159484
00:05:31.079 --> 00:05:41.799
when we are children or immature, we live in the realm of myth. We are mythological.

cue0159485
00:05:41.799 --> 00:06:04.799
We are not totally aware of either time or space. Ideas pollute our mind. And those ideas prevent us from perceiving the real reality.

cue0159486
00:06:04.799 --> 00:06:19.799
At that stage, the world is anthropocentric. What I mean to say is, man, the individual, the person, is at the center of reality.

cue0159487
00:06:19.799 --> 00:06:38.799
When the primitive man, or we, in an immature stage, perceive the reality, this reality is a projection of ourselves. Even when we love or when we hate.

cue0159488
00:06:38.799 --> 00:06:57.799
Even when we speak of God, the God that we perceive at that early stage of development is a God fabricated by our own myth, by our own imagination.

cue0159489
00:06:57.799 --> 00:07:13.799
There is another stage, and this stage of reason, of rationality. There is a stage in which we discover that there is an objective reality.

cue0159490
00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:35.799
Something that does not depend on us. Texts, that there are laws, invariable, mathematical, mechanical, that did not and will not change.

cue0159491
00:07:35.799 --> 00:07:54.799
And then we try to comprehend this world. We immerse ourselves in the world of the objective. In the world of must, of necessity, cause, effect.

cue0159492
00:07:54.799 --> 00:08:15.799
But once that we course into the realm of the objective, we come at a boundary. And that boundary is what my mind has called the realm of the mystical.

cue0159493
00:08:16.799 --> 00:08:34.799
The realm of prophecy. There is a limit to rationality. Rationality is important, is a stage in human development.

cue0159494
00:08:34.799 --> 00:08:50.799
But there is a realm, much larger and bigger and complex than the world of rationality, that transcends it.

cue0159495
00:08:50.799 --> 00:09:10.799
And when you come to that border, the rules that you had while in the realm of rationality will no longer operate.

cue0159496
00:09:10.799 --> 00:09:37.799
It is a different kind of reality. For my mind it is, the difference between the world of the mystic, in that sense, is not the world that negates rationality, but rather than transcends rationality.

cue0159497
00:09:38.799 --> 00:09:44.799
For my mind it is the Sodot, that speaks constantly, the secrets of the Tora.

cue0159498
00:09:44.799 --> 00:10:10.799
The cosmology of the Tora, the chariot of the Tora, is not an anti-rational realm, but is the realm of the post-rational.

cue0159499
00:10:10.799 --> 00:10:28.799
For reasons that really are irrelevant at this point to explain, somehow the way God programmed the human race and the human individual,

cue0159500
00:10:28.799 --> 00:10:46.799
is to evolve as an anthropological group or as an individual, from the realm of the mythical, to the realm of the rational, to the realm of the post-rational.

cue0159501
00:10:46.799 --> 00:10:57.799
For my mind it is, you can never pass from the mythical to the post-rational.

cue0159502
00:10:58.799 --> 00:11:16.799
The only way to reach mysticism, for my mind it is, the mysticism of the Tora, the mysticism of the prophets, is to exhaust your rationality.

cue0159503
00:11:17.799 --> 00:11:36.799
And when you come to the very end of what your mind can achieve, only at the border, then you can discover another realm of reality.

cue0159504
00:11:37.799 --> 00:11:58.799
But, for those who remain in the early stage of mythical thinking, the world of mysticism that they have is a figment of their own imagination.

cue0159505
00:11:59.799 --> 00:12:07.799
Let me be a little bit more articulate and precise about my mindless thinking.

cue0159506
00:12:08.799 --> 00:12:17.799
There are some very important ideas that my mindless discusses in reference to mysticism.

cue0159507
00:12:18.799 --> 00:12:32.799
Mysticism, for my mindless, is the aim, not of the Jew, but of the human race.

cue0159508
00:12:33.799 --> 00:12:49.799
It means, in different words, that mysticism is an anthropological dimension, is something that pertains to the very essence of humankind.

cue0159509
00:12:50.799 --> 00:12:55.799
That is one point, terribly important.

cue0159510
00:12:56.799 --> 00:13:15.799
Second point, the passing from the mythical to the rational, from the rational to the mystical, for my mindless, is relative to the human capacities.

cue0159511
00:13:15.799 --> 00:13:37.799
Somebody with limited education, with limited intellectual capacities, for that individual, the passing from the mythical to the rational to the mystical,

cue0159512
00:13:37.799 --> 00:13:46.799
would be different than for Sir Isaac Newton or for Dr. Albert Einstein.

cue0159513
00:13:47.799 --> 00:13:58.799
But nonetheless, each individual, within his or her own capacities, could develop.

cue0159514
00:13:59.799 --> 00:14:03.799
That is another aspect of mysticism.

cue0159515
00:14:04.799 --> 00:14:10.799
Now, I want to be more and more specific.

cue0159516
00:14:13.799 --> 00:14:29.799
Briefly, the mystic is the individual who, in a sense, discovers who he or she is.

cue0159517
00:14:30.799 --> 00:14:43.799
More precise, the mystic is the one who forges him or herself.

cue0159518
00:14:44.799 --> 00:14:47.799
Let me explain.

cue0159519
00:14:48.799 --> 00:15:10.799
For the mythical mind, for the primitive, for those who do not face reality and rationality, to always think about some idyllic past.

cue0159520
00:15:11.799 --> 00:15:14.799
The paradise in the past.

cue0159521
00:15:15.799 --> 00:15:18.799
Oh, how beautiful things were when I was a child.

cue0159522
00:15:19.799 --> 00:15:24.799
Always a past, a past, a past.

cue0159523
00:15:25.799 --> 00:15:35.799
In Christian tradition, believing Jesus in cooperation in the Corpus Christi, would take us back into the time of ʾAdam.

cue0159524
00:15:36.799 --> 00:15:52.799
For the Jew, the most important aspect of time is neither the past nor the future.

cue0159525
00:15:53.799 --> 00:15:56.799
The rabbis and my mothers emphasize,

cue0159526
00:16:01.799 --> 00:16:08.799
the most important moment is right now.

cue0159527
00:16:09.799 --> 00:16:14.799
And let me explain what does it mean there, right now.

cue0159528
00:16:15.799 --> 00:16:19.799
The moment of the present.

cue0159529
00:16:19.799 --> 00:16:32.799
If we believe that there is a God who started moving things at cosmological hour zero,

cue0159530
00:16:33.799 --> 00:16:55.799
therefore it means that every moment now is the combination, the concatation of infinite circumstances that focus all of them in this single moment.

cue0159531
00:16:56.799 --> 00:17:13.800
And right now you, as an individual, could do something that nobody else ever was able to do, and nobody again will ever be able to duplicate.

cue0159532
00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:24.800
And when you do that thing now, you change the course of the cosmos.

cue0159533
00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:32.800
And in a sense, you open new possibilities for new nows.

cue0159534
00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.800
The rabbis say,

cue0159535
00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:41.800
There is no man who does not have an hour.

cue0159536
00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:51.800
God never created a human being without giving he, she, gentile Jew, an hour.

cue0159537
00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:59.800
A moment in which he, she could do something because it's in the right place at the right time.

cue0159538
00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:05.800
And because he, she has certain experience or certain knowledge or certain thing that nobody else has.

cue0159539
00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:22.800
And when you grab the moment, you become something, someone that nobody else ever was like it or will be like it.

cue0159540
00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:29.800
You forge your individuality in that moment.

cue0159541
00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.800
The rabbis say,

cue0159542
00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:40.800
There is a man who buys his world in one hour.

cue0159543
00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:52.800
There are men, humans, and they tell a story about a gentile, about an inverted sinner Jew,

cue0159544
00:18:53.800 --> 00:19:01.800
and about an executioner, a pagan executioner.

cue0159545
00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:12.800
And these three individuals, each one in a different context, had an opportunity to do something.

cue0159546
00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:16.800
And they grabbed it.

cue0159547
00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:24.800
And they forged their own universe.

cue0159548
00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:31.800
So therefore, for my Marianist mysticism,

cue0159549
00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:36.800
we are not only studying books, of course we should read.

cue0159550
00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:40.800
The Jewish people, the Hebrew people.

cue0159551
00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.800
But all this reading and all this studying,

cue0159552
00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:53.800
they should eventually lead to a crossroad.

cue0159553
00:19:54.800 --> 00:20:01.800
The rabbis say something which baffles the mind.

cue0159554
00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.800
He says,

cue0159555
00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:09.800
How are we going to define a young sage?

cue0159556
00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:20.800
The young sage is somebody who is standing at a crossroad.

cue0159557
00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.800
What does it mean?

cue0159558
00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:31.800
Normally, we are objective.

cue0159559
00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:34.800
Oh yes.

cue0159560
00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:40.800
We follow the standard directions.

cue0159561
00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.800
We speak like everybody else.

cue0159562
00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:51.800
Statistics could tell more or less how we are going to behave.

cue0159563
00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:54.800
We are objective.

cue0159564
00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.800
They ask us a question.

cue0159565
00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.800
They know exactly what we are going to say.

cue0159566
00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:09.800
And therefore, in a sense, we are not we.

cue0159567
00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:18.800
We are the community of an intellectual movement.

cue0159568
00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.800
But we are somebody else.

cue0159569
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:27.800
A young sage, a tamichacham,

cue0159570
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:35.800
is somebody who reached the end of the road.

cue0159571
00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:40.800
And now the road bifurcates.

cue0159572
00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:47.800
And nobody else before him

cue0159573
00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:51.800
had traded this new course.

cue0159574
00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:57.800
And you have to make a decision

cue0159575
00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:01.800
which is absolutely personal.

cue0159576
00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.800
It is not objective.

cue0159577
00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:08.800
It is subjective.

cue0159578
00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:14.800
Nobody can teach you and tell you what to do.

cue0159579
00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:18.800
Because if somebody tells you what to do,

cue0159580
00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:22.800
it is not you who is doing it.

cue0159581
00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:27.800
At one moment in your life,

cue0159582
00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:32.800
you have to cut the umbilical cord.

cue0159583
00:22:33.800 --> 00:22:35.800
Take a chance.

cue0159584
00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:41.800
I may make the greatest mistake in my life,

cue0159585
00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:45.800
but I'm going to do it.

cue0159586
00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:47.800
What is going to be the result?

cue0159587
00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:50.800
I don't know.

cue0159588
00:22:53.800 --> 00:23:01.800
And you go through an uncharted road.

cue0159589
00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:07.800
Now, for my marriage,

cue0159590
00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:10.800
the mysticism of marriage is totally different

cue0159591
00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:13.800
than the qabbala mysticism.

cue0159592
00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:14.800
Why?

cue0159593
00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:17.800
For my marriage,

cue0159594
00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:20.800
if you could speak,

cue0159595
00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:24.800
if you could articulate

cue0159596
00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:27.800
your mystical experience,

cue0159597
00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.800
it is no longer mystical.

cue0159598
00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.800
If you could explain it,

cue0159599
00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:35.800
if you could say,

cue0159600
00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:38.800
why I did what I did,

cue0159601
00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:41.800
or didn't do what I didn't do,

cue0159602
00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:45.800
you are again in the world of rationality

cue0159603
00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:50.800
and you are afraid to cross the border.

cue0159604
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:53.800
So, for my marriage,

cue0159605
00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:58.800
the most important aspect of mysticism

cue0159606
00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:01.800
is not the content,

cue0159607
00:24:02.800 --> 00:24:04.800
is not the vision,

cue0159608
00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:09.800
is the idea of being alone.

cue0159609
00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:11.800
My marriage has a beautiful description.

cue0159610
00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:16.800
You are in a dense, dark night.

cue0159611
00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:19.800
You look around you

cue0159612
00:24:20.800 --> 00:24:22.800
and there is nothing that you could see.

cue0159613
00:24:23.800 --> 00:24:26.800
And you take a decision

cue0159614
00:24:27.800 --> 00:24:30.800
and somehow there is a spark.

cue0159615
00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:34.800
And you see something.

cue0159616
00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:37.800
And you see something that is out of this world

cue0159617
00:24:37.800 --> 00:24:39.800
because you cannot explain it

cue0159618
00:24:40.800 --> 00:24:42.800
in your own words.

cue0159619
00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:47.800
The spark dissipates.

cue0159620
00:24:48.800 --> 00:24:51.800
You are again in the dark.

cue0159621
00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:54.800
But you remember,

cue0159622
00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:57.800
there was a moment of illumination.

cue0159623
00:24:58.800 --> 00:25:00.800
And in that moment of illumination,

cue0159624
00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:04.800
you became you.

cue0159625
00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:09.800
Let me explain it better.

cue0159626
00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:12.800
For me,

cue0159627
00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:17.800
the key to Jewish mysticism

cue0159628
00:25:18.800 --> 00:25:20.800
is in the scripture.

cue0159629
00:25:21.800 --> 00:25:23.800
In the book of Genesis,

cue0159630
00:25:24.800 --> 00:25:28.800
when our patriarch Jacob

cue0159631
00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:32.800
pleased the Holy Land

cue0159632
00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:39.800
going to his uncle Laban,

cue0159633
00:25:40.800 --> 00:25:42.800
Jewish mysticism,

cue0159634
00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:45.800
the vision that Jacob had.

cue0159635
00:25:46.800 --> 00:25:48.800
He saw a ladder

cue0159636
00:25:49.800 --> 00:25:51.800
going all the way up to heaven.

cue0159637
00:25:52.800 --> 00:25:54.800
And lo and behold,

cue0159638
00:25:54.800 --> 00:26:06.800
we are climbing up the ladder

cue0159639
00:26:07.800 --> 00:26:09.800
and descending the ladder.

cue0159640
00:26:10.800 --> 00:26:14.800
The problem,

cue0159641
00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:20.800
what kind of angels are we talking about?

cue0159642
00:26:20.800 --> 00:26:24.800
Angels, we imagine,

cue0159643
00:26:25.800 --> 00:26:29.800
they inhabit heaven.

cue0159644
00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:33.800
If they inhabit heaven,

cue0159645
00:26:34.800 --> 00:26:36.800
then angels of God

cue0159646
00:26:37.800 --> 00:26:39.800
are first coming down

cue0159647
00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:42.800
and then going up.

cue0159648
00:26:43.800 --> 00:26:45.800
But the scripture doesn't tell you this.

cue0159649
00:26:46.800 --> 00:26:48.800
It tells you the other way around.

cue0159650
00:26:49.800 --> 00:26:51.800
[inaudible]

cue0159651
00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:54.800
אוהלים, first climb up,

cue0159652
00:26:56.800 --> 00:26:58.800
and then come down.

cue0159653
00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:03.800
Even Gaviro says something about it.

cue0159654
00:27:06.800 --> 00:27:08.800
He said it.

cue0159655
00:27:09.800 --> 00:27:11.800
And Maimonides develops it.

cue0159656
00:27:12.800 --> 00:27:15.800
The angels of God

cue0159657
00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:18.800
are we.

cue0159658
00:27:20.800 --> 00:27:22.800
Something useful.

cue0159659
00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:32.800
And you benefit

cue0159660
00:27:33.800 --> 00:27:35.800
your people

cue0159661
00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:40.800
when you translate your vision

cue0159662
00:27:41.800 --> 00:27:43.800
into something that is useful,

cue0159663
00:27:44.800 --> 00:27:46.800
that is good.

cue0159664
00:27:47.800 --> 00:27:49.800
For Maimonides,

cue0159665
00:27:50.800 --> 00:27:52.800
if you read very carefully

cue0159666
00:27:53.800 --> 00:27:55.800
the last part of the guide,

cue0159667
00:27:56.800 --> 00:27:58.800
the ultimate purpose

cue0159668
00:27:59.800 --> 00:28:01.800
of mystical vision

cue0159669
00:28:02.800 --> 00:28:04.800
is ḥesed.

cue0159670
00:28:05.800 --> 00:28:07.800
To practice

cue0159671
00:28:07.800 --> 00:28:09.800
good deeds to people.

cue0159672
00:28:11.800 --> 00:28:13.800
Good deeds to people

cue0159673
00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:16.800
is the chariot.

cue0159674
00:28:17.800 --> 00:28:20.800
Remember the chariot that Ezekiel saw

cue0159675
00:28:21.800 --> 00:28:25.800
as the temple was being destroyed in Jerusalem.

cue0159676
00:28:27.800 --> 00:28:30.800
Ezekiel sees a chariot

cue0159677
00:28:32.800 --> 00:28:34.800
full of keruvḇim,

cue0159678
00:28:34.800 --> 00:28:36.800
keruvḇim.

cue0159679
00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:40.800
For Maimonides, this is the ultimate mysticism.

cue0159680
00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:43.800
There's nothing higher than that.

cue0159681
00:28:45.800 --> 00:28:47.800
He doesn't want to tell us about

cue0159682
00:28:48.800 --> 00:28:51.800
what is the meaning of this,

cue0159683
00:28:52.800 --> 00:28:54.800
because it's forbidden, he said.

cue0159684
00:28:55.800 --> 00:28:57.800
You have to decipher on your own

cue0159685
00:28:58.800 --> 00:29:00.800
what I mean to say.

cue0159686
00:29:01.800 --> 00:29:03.800
Work your mind.

cue0159687
00:29:05.800 --> 00:29:07.800
It says two different things.

cue0159688
00:29:08.800 --> 00:29:10.800
First of all, the Merkabah,

cue0159689
00:29:11.800 --> 00:29:13.800
the chariot,

cue0159690
00:29:14.800 --> 00:29:16.800
is the cosmos.

cue0159691
00:29:18.800 --> 00:29:20.800
The universe.

cue0159692
00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:25.800
And somehow, this universe

cue0159693
00:29:26.800 --> 00:29:28.800
is being pulled

cue0159694
00:29:29.800 --> 00:29:31.800
by keruvḇim.

cue0159695
00:29:32.800 --> 00:29:34.800
Now, mind you,

cue0159696
00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:38.800
in Hebrew, you write

cue0159697
00:29:39.800 --> 00:29:41.800
kerub,

cue0159698
00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:45.800
kaf, resh, vav, bed.

cue0159699
00:29:46.800 --> 00:29:48.800
That's the way you write it.

cue0159700
00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:51.800
In another place,

cue0159701
00:29:52.800 --> 00:29:54.800
Maimonides speaks about many things

cue0159702
00:29:55.800 --> 00:29:57.800
and then says, well,

cue0159703
00:29:58.800 --> 00:30:00.800
you have to know that sometimes

cue0159704
00:30:01.800 --> 00:30:03.800
in Hebrew,

cue0159705
00:30:04.800 --> 00:30:06.800
letters change their orders.

cue0159706
00:30:07.800 --> 00:30:09.800
And there's many words in Hebrew like

cue0159707
00:30:10.800 --> 00:30:12.800
keves, kesev, you know.

cue0159708
00:30:13.800 --> 00:30:15.800
Let me tell you my interpretation.

cue0159709
00:30:16.800 --> 00:30:18.800
Is it the correct one?

cue0159710
00:30:19.800 --> 00:30:21.800
I don't know. It's a subjective interpretation.

cue0159711
00:30:22.800 --> 00:30:24.800
All right.

cue0159712
00:30:25.800 --> 00:30:28.800
I think that what Maimonides wants to tell us

cue0159713
00:30:28.800 --> 00:30:30.800
is that the word kerub

cue0159714
00:30:31.800 --> 00:30:33.800
means Rahub.

cue0159715
00:30:34.800 --> 00:30:36.800
What does it mean, Rahub?

cue0159716
00:30:37.800 --> 00:30:39.800
In other places, it speaks about

cue0159717
00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:42.800
God, Roheb,

cue0159718
00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:45.800
Mount,

cue0159719
00:30:46.800 --> 00:30:48.800
the Arabot, the universe.

cue0159720
00:30:52.800 --> 00:30:54.800
In another place, he tells us

cue0159721
00:30:55.800 --> 00:30:57.800
that the kerub

cue0159722
00:30:58.800 --> 00:31:00.800
is the faces of innocent little children.

cue0159723
00:31:02.800 --> 00:31:04.800
I think

cue0159724
00:31:05.800 --> 00:31:07.800
they are the angels of the Lord

cue0159725
00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:10.800
because they carry

cue0159726
00:31:11.800 --> 00:31:13.800
on earth

cue0159727
00:31:14.800 --> 00:31:16.800
the divine plan.

cue0159728
00:31:18.800 --> 00:31:20.800
That is something unique.

cue0159729
00:31:21.800 --> 00:31:23.800
Perhaps only you

cue0159730
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:26.800
could have that time

cue0159731
00:31:26.800 --> 00:31:28.800
to make that lemon pie

cue0159732
00:31:29.800 --> 00:31:31.800
that fed that hungry man

cue0159733
00:31:32.800 --> 00:31:34.800
that did this, that did that

cue0159734
00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:37.800
that saved the universe.

cue0159735
00:31:38.800 --> 00:31:40.800
We don't know.

cue0159736
00:31:41.800 --> 00:31:43.800
You moved

cue0159737
00:31:44.800 --> 00:31:46.800
something in some direction.

cue0159738
00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:48.800
Yes?

cue0159739
00:31:49.800 --> 00:31:51.800
And you became the kerub

cue0159740
00:31:52.800 --> 00:31:54.800
that God was mounting.

cue0159741
00:31:55.800 --> 00:31:57.800
It is discussed by many Jewish scholars.

cue0159742
00:31:59.800 --> 00:32:03.800
Asher bara ʾElohim la'asot.

cue0159743
00:32:04.800 --> 00:32:07.800
The universe, the cosmos.

cue0159744
00:32:10.800 --> 00:32:12.800
God created it

cue0159745
00:32:13.800 --> 00:32:15.800
la'asot.

cue0159746
00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:17.800
So we do.

cue0159747
00:32:18.800 --> 00:32:19.800
We complete it.

cue0159748
00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:22.800
We carry the universe

cue0159749
00:32:22.800 --> 00:32:25.800
in a particular direction.

cue0159750
00:32:26.800 --> 00:32:28.800
And we do this

cue0159751
00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:31.800
by seeing something.

cue0159752
00:32:32.800 --> 00:32:35.800
And translate that thought

cue0159753
00:32:37.800 --> 00:32:40.800
into an act of loving kindness.

cue0159754
00:32:41.800 --> 00:32:43.800
Then we become the kerub of God.

cue0159755
00:32:44.800 --> 00:32:45.800
We are the keruvḇim.

cue0159756
00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:47.800
We are the angels

cue0159757
00:32:48.800 --> 00:32:50.800
going up and down.

cue0159758
00:32:51.800 --> 00:32:53.800
And this world

cue0159759
00:32:54.800 --> 00:32:56.800
becomes a better world.

cue0159760
00:32:57.800 --> 00:32:59.800
I want to illustrate

cue0159761
00:33:00.800 --> 00:33:02.800
my whole theory.

cue0159762
00:33:04.800 --> 00:33:06.800
Historical fact.

cue0159763
00:33:07.800 --> 00:33:11.800
People speak about Maimonides, the philosophers are nonsense.

cue0159764
00:33:12.800 --> 00:33:15.800
He was a physician

cue0159765
00:33:16.800 --> 00:33:19.800
a very wealthy and successful businessman.

cue0159766
00:33:20.800 --> 00:33:22.800
I think he was the wealthiest man of his time

cue0159767
00:33:23.800 --> 00:33:25.800
among the Jews, certainly.

cue0159768
00:33:26.800 --> 00:33:27.800
And

cue0159769
00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:30.800
there is a letter

cue0159770
00:33:31.800 --> 00:33:32.800
written by

cue0159771
00:33:33.800 --> 00:33:36.800
Chemuevi Mintibon from Provence, France.

cue0159772
00:33:37.800 --> 00:33:39.800
He wanted to translate, he was a translator of

cue0159773
00:33:40.800 --> 00:33:42.800
the Moreh Neḇukhim from the Arabic into Hebrew.

cue0159774
00:33:43.800 --> 00:33:44.800
And he says,

cue0159775
00:33:45.800 --> 00:33:48.800
ask Maimonides, please I want to come to see you and speak to you.

cue0159776
00:33:48.800 --> 00:33:50.800
Maimonides says, no, don't come.

cue0159777
00:33:51.800 --> 00:33:52.800
I'm busy.

cue0159778
00:33:53.800 --> 00:33:55.800
And he tells him exactly what he was doing.

cue0159779
00:33:56.800 --> 00:33:58.800
And the most important thing for me

cue0159780
00:33:59.800 --> 00:34:00.800
is that after

cue0159781
00:34:01.800 --> 00:34:03.800
a very hard day at the palace of the king

cue0159782
00:34:04.800 --> 00:34:06.800
he says, I would come home

cue0159783
00:34:09.800 --> 00:34:11.800
and hundreds of people

cue0159784
00:34:12.800 --> 00:34:14.800
would be waiting.

cue0159785
00:34:15.800 --> 00:34:17.800
Jews, Christians

cue0159786
00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:21.800
pagans, there were in Egypt pagans

cue0159787
00:34:22.800 --> 00:34:24.800
black individuals who were taken as slaves.

cue0159788
00:34:25.800 --> 00:34:26.800
Jews

cue0159789
00:34:27.800 --> 00:34:29.800
and they're waiting for me

cue0159790
00:34:30.800 --> 00:34:32.800
to administer medicine to them.

cue0159791
00:34:33.800 --> 00:34:35.800
And Maimonides says, I will be exhausted

cue0159792
00:34:36.800 --> 00:34:38.800
and sometimes I have to examine the patients.

cue0159793
00:34:40.800 --> 00:34:43.800
While I'm lying in bed

cue0159794
00:34:44.800 --> 00:34:46.800
I simply don't have the energy.

cue0159795
00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:49.800
And Maimonides devoted

cue0159796
00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:53.800
the last years of his life

cue0159797
00:34:56.800 --> 00:34:58.800
to help people.

cue0159798
00:34:59.800 --> 00:35:01.800
To help people.

cue0159799
00:35:02.800 --> 00:35:03.800
Not Jews.

cue0159800
00:35:04.800 --> 00:35:05.800
Not Christians.

cue0159801
00:35:06.800 --> 00:35:07.800
Not Muslims.

cue0159802
00:35:08.800 --> 00:35:09.800
People.

cue0159803
00:35:11.800 --> 00:35:13.800
And he died because of this.

cue0159804
00:35:14.800 --> 00:35:16.800
We know exactly the situation in which he died.

cue0159805
00:35:17.800 --> 00:35:19.800
A plague broke in Egypt.

cue0159806
00:35:21.800 --> 00:35:23.800
He went out

cue0159807
00:35:24.800 --> 00:35:25.800
to assist his patients.

cue0159808
00:35:26.800 --> 00:35:27.800
Gratis, of course.

cue0159809
00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:29.800
He believed that

cue0159810
00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:32.800
medicine should be freely administered

cue0159811
00:35:33.800 --> 00:35:35.800
especially to the poor.

cue0159812
00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:38.800
He contracted whatever the plague was

cue0159813
00:35:39.800 --> 00:35:40.800
and he died.

cue0159814
00:35:41.800 --> 00:35:42.800
So

cue0159815
00:35:43.800 --> 00:35:45.800
I know about the other mystical schools.

cue0159816
00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:47.800
I still believe

cue0159817
00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:49.800
that there is room

cue0159818
00:35:50.800 --> 00:35:51.800
to investigate

cue0159819
00:35:52.800 --> 00:35:54.800
the mysticism of Maimonides.

cue0159820
00:35:55.800 --> 00:35:58.800
Post-modern rational man

cue0159821
00:35:59.800 --> 00:36:02.800
that knows somehow subjectively

cue0159822
00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:05.800
that at this moment

cue0159823
00:36:06.800 --> 00:36:07.800
now

cue0159824
00:36:07.800 --> 00:36:10.800
there is something that he, she could do

cue0159825
00:36:11.800 --> 00:36:13.800
that nobody else does it.

cue0159826
00:36:14.800 --> 00:36:16.800
The mystic is the one

cue0159827
00:36:17.800 --> 00:36:19.800
who grabs the now

cue0159828
00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:22.800
brings it down to earth

cue0159829
00:36:23.800 --> 00:36:24.800
and thus become

cue0159830
00:36:25.800 --> 00:36:26.800
the keruvḇim

cue0159831
00:36:27.800 --> 00:36:28.800
of God, the angel.

cue0159832
00:36:29.800 --> 00:36:31.800
Pushing, pulling this cosmos

cue0159833
00:36:32.800 --> 00:36:33.800
to a better destiny.

cue0159834
00:36:34.800 --> 00:36:36.800
Thank you for your attention

cue0159835
00:36:37.800 --> 00:36:39.800
and I hope I have questions.

cue0159836
00:36:40.800 --> 00:36:41.800
Thank you very much.

cue0159837
00:36:44.800 --> 00:36:46.800
I'm going to have somebody monitor the questions.

cue0159838
00:36:54.800 --> 00:36:56.800
I tell you why the matter is

cue0159839
00:36:57.800 --> 00:36:58.800
the chariot is a matter of secrecy.

cue0159840
00:36:59.800 --> 00:37:01.800
Because you cannot understand

cue0159841
00:37:02.800 --> 00:37:03.800
who you are.

cue0159842
00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:05.800
Oh yes.

cue0159843
00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:08.800
The question that I was asked

cue0159844
00:37:09.800 --> 00:37:10.800
such a simple doctrine.

cue0159845
00:37:11.800 --> 00:37:12.800
Why is

cue0159846
00:37:13.800 --> 00:37:15.800
an esoteric, mystical

cue0159847
00:37:17.800 --> 00:37:18.800
doctrine

cue0159848
00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:20.800
is very important.

cue0159849
00:37:21.800 --> 00:37:24.800
Because in order to discover yourself

cue0159850
00:37:26.800 --> 00:37:29.800
to discover really who you are

cue0159851
00:37:29.800 --> 00:37:31.800
you must transcend

cue0159852
00:37:34.800 --> 00:37:36.800
the world of mythology

cue0159853
00:37:37.800 --> 00:37:39.800
just as part of our youth.

cue0159854
00:37:41.800 --> 00:37:43.800
My mother is considered mythology

cue0159855
00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:46.800
mythological thinking

cue0159856
00:37:47.800 --> 00:37:49.800
part of the pagan world.

cue0159857
00:37:50.800 --> 00:37:51.800
We Jews

cue0159858
00:37:52.800 --> 00:37:54.800
also were part of pagan humanity.

cue0159859
00:37:55.800 --> 00:37:57.800
We say this in the night of the Seder

cue0159860
00:37:57.800 --> 00:37:58.800
in the night of the Seder

cue0159861
00:37:59.800 --> 00:38:00.800
Abadima'inu

cue0159862
00:38:01.800 --> 00:38:02.800
Mithila'u

cue0159863
00:38:03.800 --> 00:38:04.800
Abadha'zara

cue0159864
00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:07.800
Our ancestors also were idol worshippers.

cue0159865
00:38:08.800 --> 00:38:10.800
We must transcend this.

cue0159866
00:38:11.800 --> 00:38:13.800
There is a process

cue0159867
00:38:16.800 --> 00:38:18.800
and only at the end of the process

cue0159868
00:38:20.800 --> 00:38:22.800
after you saw the dark

cue0159869
00:38:25.800 --> 00:38:26.800
you realize

cue0159870
00:38:27.800 --> 00:38:28.800
the limits

cue0159871
00:38:29.800 --> 00:38:31.800
of your rationality

cue0159872
00:38:33.800 --> 00:38:34.800
then

cue0159873
00:38:36.800 --> 00:38:37.800
you could

cue0159874
00:38:38.800 --> 00:38:40.800
begin to fathom

cue0159875
00:38:42.800 --> 00:38:43.800
the special world

cue0159876
00:38:44.800 --> 00:38:45.800
the world transcending

cue0159877
00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:47.800
the normative.

cue0159878
00:38:48.800 --> 00:38:49.800
So

cue0159879
00:38:50.800 --> 00:38:51.800
it is a process.

cue0159880
00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:55.800
And we cannot jump into it.

cue0159881
00:38:56.800 --> 00:38:58.800
We cannot become mystical

cue0159882
00:38:59.800 --> 00:39:01.800
before sharing the mythical.

cue0159883
00:39:02.800 --> 00:39:04.800
And we cannot become mystical

cue0159884
00:39:05.800 --> 00:39:07.800
before entering and exploiting

cue0159885
00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:10.800
and exhausting rationality.

cue0159886
00:39:11.800 --> 00:39:12.800
It is a process.

cue0159887
00:39:13.800 --> 00:39:15.800
Now, again, the process for every individual is different

cue0159888
00:39:16.800 --> 00:39:18.800
according to culture, mental capacity, etc.

cue0159889
00:39:19.800 --> 00:39:20.800
But there is a process.

cue0159890
00:39:21.800 --> 00:39:23.800
And this, for my manners, is the secret of the Tora.

cue0159891
00:39:23.800 --> 00:39:25.800
The Tora, for my manners, is the system

cue0159892
00:39:26.800 --> 00:39:28.800
that helps the individual

cue0159893
00:39:29.800 --> 00:39:30.800
from the very beginning

cue0159894
00:39:31.800 --> 00:39:32.800
takes him by the hand

cue0159895
00:39:33.800 --> 00:39:35.800
until he, she

cue0159896
00:39:36.800 --> 00:39:37.800
find themselves

cue0159897
00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:40.800
at the end of the rational world

cue0159898
00:39:41.800 --> 00:39:42.800
and then they have a glimpse

cue0159899
00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:45.800
of something beyond their rationality.

cue0159900
00:39:48.800 --> 00:39:49.800
I tell you why.

cue0159901
00:39:50.800 --> 00:39:51.800
No, I don't think

cue0159902
00:39:51.800 --> 00:39:53.800
Let me repeat the question.

cue0159903
00:39:54.800 --> 00:39:55.800
Is there any parallel between

cue0159904
00:39:56.800 --> 00:39:57.800
the Buddhist nirvana

cue0159905
00:39:58.800 --> 00:39:59.800
and the

cue0159906
00:40:00.800 --> 00:40:01.800
concept of illumination

cue0159907
00:40:02.800 --> 00:40:03.800
which is in the rabbis

cue0159908
00:40:04.800 --> 00:40:05.800
and Jewish mysticism and so on.

cue0159909
00:40:06.800 --> 00:40:07.800
My manners speak about it. No.

cue0159910
00:40:08.800 --> 00:40:09.800
And I tell you why.

cue0159911
00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:11.800
Nirvana

cue0159912
00:40:12.800 --> 00:40:13.800
Buddhism

cue0159913
00:40:14.800 --> 00:40:15.800
negates

cue0159914
00:40:16.800 --> 00:40:17.800
this world.

cue0159915
00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:19.800
It's a negation of this world.

cue0159916
00:40:19.800 --> 00:40:20.800
In a sense

cue0159917
00:40:21.800 --> 00:40:22.800
it's a killing

cue0159918
00:40:23.800 --> 00:40:25.800
of the simple common human.

cue0159919
00:40:27.800 --> 00:40:29.800
And therefore, and only then

cue0159920
00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:34.800
can the light be perceived.

cue0159921
00:40:35.800 --> 00:40:37.800
In the scripture, there is a fantastic idea

cue0159922
00:40:38.800 --> 00:40:41.800
that it needs to be exploited more and more

cue0159923
00:40:42.800 --> 00:40:43.800
and more and more.

cue0159924
00:40:44.800 --> 00:40:45.800
Namely,

cue0159925
00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:47.800
that every person

cue0159926
00:40:47.800 --> 00:40:49.800
is created with the image of God.

cue0159927
00:40:50.800 --> 00:40:51.800
We have the image of God

cue0159928
00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:53.800
within us.

cue0159929
00:40:54.800 --> 00:40:55.800
And therefore,

cue0159930
00:40:56.800 --> 00:40:59.800
we don't have to annihilate ourselves.

cue0159931
00:41:00.800 --> 00:41:02.800
It's exactly the contrary.

cue0159932
00:41:03.800 --> 00:41:04.800
To develop ourselves.

cue0159933
00:41:05.800 --> 00:41:06.800
To know ourselves.

cue0159934
00:41:07.800 --> 00:41:08.800
To be

cue0159935
00:41:09.800 --> 00:41:10.800
in a sense like God

cue0159936
00:41:11.800 --> 00:41:12.800
in the sense that God is unique

cue0159937
00:41:13.800 --> 00:41:14.800
and to see the uniqueness of ourselves.

cue0159938
00:41:15.800 --> 00:41:16.800
Each one

cue0159939
00:41:17.800 --> 00:41:18.800
each person

cue0159940
00:41:19.800 --> 00:41:20.800
ever created

cue0159941
00:41:21.800 --> 00:41:22.800
or that will be created

cue0159942
00:41:23.800 --> 00:41:24.800
it has a purpose, a function

cue0159943
00:41:25.800 --> 00:41:26.800
that only he, she

cue0159944
00:41:27.800 --> 00:41:28.800
at that particular moment

cue0159945
00:41:29.800 --> 00:41:30.800
of history

cue0159946
00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:32.800
could do.

cue0159947
00:41:33.800 --> 00:41:34.800
And that is, makes us something

cue0159948
00:41:35.800 --> 00:41:36.800
which is unique by being ourselves

cue0159949
00:41:37.800 --> 00:41:38.800
not by annihilating ourselves.

cue0159950
00:41:39.800 --> 00:41:40.800
I think the difference is very important

cue0159951
00:41:41.800 --> 00:41:42.800
in that sense.

cue0159952
00:41:43.800 --> 00:41:44.800
Yes, ma'am.

cue0159953
00:41:47.800 --> 00:41:48.800
I'm going to give you an example.

cue0159954
00:41:49.800 --> 00:41:50.800
The best thing to remember.

cue0159955
00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:52.800
For my managers

cue0159956
00:41:53.800 --> 00:41:54.800
the most important thing is not to have a vision

cue0159957
00:41:55.800 --> 00:41:56.800
and, I don't know,

cue0159958
00:41:57.800 --> 00:41:58.800
be out of focus for a couple of days

cue0159959
00:41:59.800 --> 00:42:00.800
and, you know, you don't know what's coming.

cue0159960
00:42:01.800 --> 00:42:02.800
That's not a vision.

cue0159961
00:42:03.800 --> 00:42:04.800
It's to have a vision.

cue0159962
00:42:06.800 --> 00:42:08.800
And you have the intelligence

cue0159963
00:42:10.800 --> 00:42:12.800
to translate it into something

cue0159964
00:42:13.800 --> 00:42:14.800
that revolutionizes the world.

cue0159965
00:42:15.800 --> 00:42:16.800
That's something.

cue0159966
00:42:17.800 --> 00:42:18.800
Thank you.
